WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.141
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Beautiful Oops.

00:00:14.141 --> 00:00:20.282
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:20.282 --> 00:00:23.966
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:27.650
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:36.247
Sooner or later, every maker meets an oops. A spill. A drip. A tear. A color that lands in the wrong place.

00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:46.073
And an oops brings a feeling with it. Frustration. Embarrassment. The strong wish to crumple the whole page into a ball.

00:00:46.073 --> 00:00:57.126
That feeling is allowed to be here first. Nothing in this tool will hurry you past it. Feelings are not the problem. They are just the first part.

00:00:57.126 --> 00:01:02.039
When you are ready — only when you are ready — there is a question an oops can ask. Let me show you.

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:13.092
The question is this: what could this become? Not how do I hide it. Not how do I undo it. What could it become?

00:01:13.092 --> 00:01:24.145
Look at the oops the way you would look at a cloud. A drip has a shape. A tear has an edge. A splash has a direction it wanted to go.

00:01:24.145 --> 00:01:35.199
Turn the page a little. Add one line. Add one more. The oops becomes the start of something nobody planned — not even you.

00:01:35.199 --> 00:01:45.024
Here is the rule that keeps this kind: the oops you transform is your own. You never draw on, fix, or decorate a classmate's work — unless they clearly say yes.

00:01:45.024 --> 00:01:46.252
Their oops belongs to them, the same way yours belongs to you. An offer can be made. An answer of no ends it, kindly and completely.

00:01:46.252 --> 00:01:57.305
And hear this, because it is just as true: not every oops has to become art. Some oopses just get cleaned up.

00:01:57.305 --> 00:02:08.359
Some get a fresh page, and a fresh page is a fine, honest answer. Transforming is an offer this tool makes. It is never an order.

00:02:08.359 --> 00:02:16.956
Nobody ranks oopses here. Nobody compares them, and nobody shows theirs off against anyone else's. An oops is not a contest.

00:02:16.956 --> 00:02:18.184
Yours happened. You felt what you felt. And you get to choose what happens next. That choosing is the real skill, and it is already yours.

00:02:18.184 --> 00:02:26.781
Feel it first. Then choose. What could this become?

00:02:26.781 --> 00:02:32.922
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:37.834
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:43.975
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:43.975 --> 00:02:50.116
You're ready for what's next.
